1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,282
Four SpaceX tokens trade on Solana today.

2
00:00:03,832 --> 00:00:06,592
In a wallet they look identical. They are not.

3
00:00:07,142 --> 00:00:11,582
One is a real share. One expires worthless in March twenty twenty seven.

4
00:00:22,330 --> 00:00:24,370
Search a company, not a ticker.

5
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:28,424
Claim groups every token that references the same security.

6
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:35,546
Each one is graded on the legal claim behind it, not its price.

7
00:00:36,096 --> 00:00:40,920
Backpack, grade A: real shares in custody you can move to a brokerage.

8
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:46,962
Every finding carries the issuer's own words and a link to them.

9
00:00:47,512 --> 00:00:53,056
A permanent delegate that can take the token from your wallet. The key is on screen — check it yourself.

10
00:00:57,130 --> 00:01:01,618
Where a stronger claim exists and can be reached, Claim offers the move.

11
00:01:02,168 --> 00:01:06,608
The review page shows what you gain and what you give up, before a wallet opens.

12
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:16,914
Connect any wallet. Phantom, Solflare, Backpack or Trust.

13
00:01:17,464 --> 00:01:22,384
Claim never holds a key and never submits. Your wallet signs, or nothing happens.

14
00:01:23,784 --> 00:01:27,072
You can also just buy a company, and let Claim pick the token.

15
00:01:27,622 --> 00:01:30,550
A hundred and fifty four are reachable by a swap.

16
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:35,036
For eighty three, the strongest claim is not the one on sale.

17
00:01:37,144 --> 00:01:40,648
So Claim says so, in front of you, before you sign.

18
00:01:41,198 --> 00:01:45,758
The stronger Apple claim exists. It is not traded. Here is who issues it.

19
00:01:47,264 --> 00:01:51,752
Paste a wallet and every position in it is graded, worst claim first.

20
00:01:52,302 --> 00:01:54,582
What you can act on right now sits at the top.

21
00:02:06,424 --> 00:02:10,264
And the same verdict, free, over a public A P I.
